       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Metformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is double the labeled maximum daily dose of 2,550 mg for immediate-release metformin in adults. It is also well above the 2,000 mg/day maximum for extended-release. A dose that high raises the risk of GI toxicity and lactic acidosis, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nThis may be a typo. Here are some common options:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day), the maximum for immediate-release.\n- **1,000 mg PO twice daily with meals** (2,000 mg/day).\n- **500 mg or 850 mg PO** at a different frequency, if you're titrating up.\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want and I'll enter it. If you really do need a dose above the labeled maximum, that has to go through pharmacy or a prescriber override outside this system. I can't enter it on a verbal confirmation."
      }
